{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed","id":473626,"title":"Could anyone please give me a quick rundown of Kindred politics in 2ed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-08T19:04:50-07:00","id":473626,"title":"Could anyone please give me a quick rundown of Kindred politics in 2ed?","content":"I am new to V:tR and would like to better understand the political systems vampires use, such as positions and duties. Any interesting tidbits or realizations you have had about this subject could also help. Thanks in advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:44:12-07:00","id":473686,"title":"","content":"The honest answer is: it depends on the domain.<br /> <br /> Each domain is a potentially unique entity in both composition with regards to Clan and Covenant, and governing structure between them all.<br /> <br /> For instance, Tokyo's only example of one of the five conventional Covenants is the Lancea et Sanctum. Everyone else is either unaligned (a minority) or part of one of three vampire-run Zaibatsu corporations (the majority).<br /> <br /> Swansea, Wales on the other hand sorta has Covenants, but they are mostly irrelevant. Everything is controlled by a Clan Council made up of elders from each of Swansea's four Clans. I say four because they exiled and outlawed the Ventrue decades ago due to Ventrue association with oppressive industrial interests that the mostly working-class vampires of the other clans were not fond of.<br /> <br /> My best general advice would be to refer to the section starting on page 65 titled 'The City as State' in the Vampire the Requiem: Second Edition corebook. After digesting what you find there I would look at the example domains in Chapter 6, and then if none of those fit what you like you can take the material from them and the overview given under The City as State and come up with your own way of doing things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T21:06:14-07:00","id":473812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed#post473626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am new to V:tR and would like to better understand the political systems vampires use, such as positions and duties. Any interesting tidbits or realizations you have had about this subject could also help. Thanks in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lancea Sanctum</b> = Self appointed &quot;adversaries&quot; to scare people into a life of piety and devotion to god. Basically, they've taken on Satan's role to tempt mortals and punish them for giving into their selfish desires.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ordo Dracul</b> = Screw politics, they've got more important things to focus on. Like becoming the ultimate predator.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Circle of the Crone</b> = Neo Pagans and blood mages... I don't know much else beyond that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Invictus</b> = Things were better in my day, sonny! New Camarilla, plain and simple.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Carthians</b> = Try to adapt Kindred society to be more relevant with modern day forms of government.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-09-2015, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T21:42:53-07:00","id":473847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=473812#post473812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Lancea Sanctum</b> = Self appointed &quot;adversaries&quot; to scare people into a life of piety and devotion to god. Basically, they've taken on Satan's role to tempt mortals and punish them for giving into their selfish desires.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ordo Dracul</b> = Screw politics, they've got more important things to focus on. Like becoming the ultimate predator.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Circle of the Crone</b> = Neo Pagans and blood mages... I don't know much else beyond that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Invictus</b> = Things were better in my day, sonny! New Camarilla, plain and simple.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Carthians</b> = Try to adapt Kindred society to be more relevant with modern day forms of government.</div> </div> </div> </div>These stereotypes are very 1st edition. The Covenants have changed somewhat as of 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lancea et Sanctum</b> (now featuring grammatically correct Latin!) do retain the &quot;Damned by God to tempt the faithful&quot; aspect, but have also picked up a role as historians and lorekeepers. Now that the Fog of Ages is no longer a major concern, they have to work much harder to make sure <i>their</i> version of history is the one that people remember. They seek out and hoard historical documents, making the ones that support their doctrine available and well-known, and keeping those that do not under lock and key.<br /> <br /> <b>The Ordo Dracul</b> have a renewed emphasis on their defiance of the curse. Whether an individual Dragon believes the Kindred are damned by God, afflicted with some kind of supernatural virus, or something else entirely, they endeavor not just to cure themselves of the curse, but to turn it into a blessing. Not to rid themselves of the weaknesses inherent in the vampiric condition, but to use those weaknesses to their advantage.<br /> <br /> <b>The Circle of the Crone</b> have a much more specific identity now, with clearly defined origins a little under 200 years ago in Scotland and Ireland when the Lancea et Sanctum was ruthlessly persecuting pagan coteries. They banded together for mutual safety, fighting back against their oppressors. Tonight, they stand not so much as a single organized religion, but as a coalition of spiritual vampires who do not conform to the dominant Lancea et Sanctum ideology.<br /> <br /> <b>The Invictus</b> give no shits for tradition or the old ways. The Camarilla fell because it refused to adapt to changing times, and the Invictus, while they consider themselves the spiritual successors to the Camarilla, are not going to make the same mistake again. They are about power and control, by any means - old or new. They have also picked up some new themes as the self-styled enforcers of the Masquerade. One of their new nicknames is &quot;the conspiracy of silence.&quot; They're the ones who make the people who know too much disappear, and the people who say too much public examples.<br /> <br /> <b>The Carthian Movement</b> is analogous to the Circle of the Crone in that they are not one single political ideology, but more of a support network of political dissidents of various leanings united against the dominant Invictus power. They may not all agree on what to <i>do</i> once that power is overthrown, but to The Firebrands, that's secondary. What matters most is what's right here, right now, and right now, the Kindred need a revolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T21:51:29-07:00","id":473853,"title":"","content":"It really does depend, but in first edition there were a lot of options made available with the covenant books. I don't have them all and I don't remember everything from the ones I have read so this may be not entirely correct.<br /> <br /> I think the Ordo Dracul went into the most detail. New members usually start off all alone but at some point are ideally picked by a mentor, at which point they become a more vital member of the clan. The mentor and apprentice relationship seems pretty tight, and something they take seriously, its really good for storytelling opportunities as well. An Ordo Dracul Prince is called a Master. They are divided into, primarily, three groups. The Sworn of the Dying Light, who are the scholars, the Sworn of the Axe, who are the warriors, and the Sworn of the Mysteries, who act as diplomats to the other covenants and politicians in their own. There are a couple other types of Sworn, but I think they're considered dead or heretical in modern nights. The Sworn of the Locust is one. The Ordo also have these long, encoded titles that tell other people in the know how many coils they've mastered and which ones they're the best at. There's also this one member of the covenant who knows all the secrets, I think they're called the Kogaion. They know what everyone is studying, the locations of all the wyrms nests and members of the covenant in the area. Because of this they aren't allowed to show up at big meetings where the heads of the Sworn are, because losing the Kogaion and the heads would be devastating to the covenant.<br /> <br /> I wasn't sure if this was how their politics worked or just how they loosely organized, but I think the Circle of the Crone based themselves off of archetypes. I think the leader of the Circle of the Crone is called a Heirophant. I forget all the archetypes, but there's the Hero, who takes up the heroes of old archetype where they're not necessarily a good person but more of a loner who does what needs to be done. The Father, which is an evolution of the Hero, who has learned from their experiences and settled down to be a mentor and advisor to the young. The Scarlet Woman, who sort of stands outside their normal social statuses and cleaves to her own ethical and philosophical beliefs. The Fool, who is sort of like the trickster, they poke at rules and rulemakers, sort of acting as a devil's advocate so crones remember to see other points of view. And the Maiden, who is the 'virgin,' in that she has not killed a person, she's still untouched by that part of vampire life. There's more that I can't recall offhand, but it was an interesting read. There was another position that was sort of like the Ordo's Kogaion, the Rex Nemorensis, who are the keepers of forbidden knowledge.<br /> <br /> Other than that, the 'standard' vampire city has a Prince, who rules, and a Sheriff, who enforces the law. Ideally they're neutral, more loyal to the law than the Prince but how likely is that? There's a primogen council, who are supposed to be the advisors to the Prince though they may not share the Prince's goals. Some might be given jobs similar to a Minister in some government systems, such as Norris in Chicago,who acted as the Prince's spymaster. Alternatively they could be the true power behind a puppet Prince. Clans might have a priscus, a particularly powerful member of a clan that may sort of act as leader or spokesperson for it, I think that would be traditionally separate from covenant activities but I guess a priscus in a covenant would be a good way to get a lot of similar vampires in it. There's a Master of Elysium, who runs, organized and maintains the Elysium. Harpies, who are sort of like gossip mongers, they get the word out about orders from up top, but can also be used for spreading rumors or gathering information, they tend to have their finger on the pulse of vampire society, again, ideally. The Prince and the primogen might also have Hounds, who are sort of like, I guess, adventurers? They do the gruntwork, whether it's roughing up people, spying, spreading lies and staking liars, they tend to be loyal to their master and the rest of society might not know if they're Hounds or who they're working for.<br /> <br /> I've probably left out a lot and got a lot wrong but I'm sure someone will add and correct things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T23:22:54-07:00","id":473926,"title":"","content":"Specific titles and duties time! In all cases, keep in mind that these are only examples of ways a Covenant might (stereo)typically be organized, and may be completely different in any given domain. <br /> <br /> Carthian Movement:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>The Prefect</b> is the official representative of The Revolution. Usually elected, the Prefect's job is to play nice with the other covenants, present a respectable face for the movement so the other members will at least be tolerated within the city, and to act as a sort of figurehead so the other factions have a face they associate with the Movement and feel safer for it.<br /> <br /> <b>The Myrmadon</b> is the arbiter of the internal disputes that inevitably arise within a covenant of Kindred who basically only work together because they all agree the current system doesn't work. When you've got a Marxist member and a Neo-Platonic member at each other's throats, it's the Myrmadon's job to break it up.<br /> <br /> That's about as much official structure as most Carthians are comfortable with, though some domains where the local Carthians' ideals are unusually closely aligned may have more. Look to human political structures for examples.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Circle of the Crone:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>The Heirophant</b> or <b>The High Priestess</b> is the lead ritualist. He or she is the spiritual leader of the local Acolytes, offering guidance to those who seek it, and presiding over most Cruac rituals.<br /> <br /> <b>The Chorus</b> is a catch-all term for new initiates who have not been taught the secrets of Cruac.<br /> <br /> <b>Rex Nemoranses</b> is an outdated title that rarely ever sees use in modern nights. Historically, it was held by the eldest member, and it was this Kindred's job to act as an un-living repository of forbidden knowledge.<br /> <br /> Like the Carthian Movement, the Circle of the Crone is big on personal freedom and not so big on structure and organization, so this is the extent of their &quot;official&quot; titles. However, they often hold ideas of philosophical roles. They have no associated duties, and are not held by individuals, they are more like descriptors of where a member is at in her un-life. Every member therefore fits into one philosophical role or another. These vary greatly from one domain to the next depending on local beliefs and customs, but one common philosophical structure is the family roles.<br /> <br /> <b>The Fool</b> is an Acolyte, typically male, who is unenlightened in the ways of the Circle. Their naivete is valued, as it offers a certain insight that the jaded elder members might miss. Fools are occasionally called upon to come up with ideas so crazy they just might work.<br /> <br /> <b>The Maiden</b> or <b>The Virgin</b> is the typically female counterpart to the Fool, often young, and always ignorant of any Cruac. They are valued for their purity, as Cruac takes its toll on a ritualist's Humanity. Virgins are often called upon to act as Touchstones for degenerating ritualists. (Ok, ok, the Touchstone mechanic didn't actually exist yet when the book this is from was written, but they serve as anchors to keep the low-Humanity members from going off the deep end, and that's exactly what Touchstones do.)<br /> <br /> <b>The Hero</b> is the spiritually adolescent role aligned with typically masculine ideals. Heroes go on quests to prove themselves and to earn favor. They're the go-to foot soldiers of the Covenant.<br /> <br /> <b>The Whore</b> is the typically feminine counterpart to the Hero. Whores challenge tradition and make their own way. They are seen as a much-needed counterpoint to the elders who can get stuck in their ways.<br /> <br /> <b>The Father</b> is a spiritually mature masculine figure who guides less mature Acolytes, typically through discipline.<br /> <br /> <b>The Mother</b> is a spiritually mature feminine figure who guides through praise.<br /> <br /> <b>The Hermit</b> is an elder member, usually male and always of high enough Blood Potency that they must feed on vampires, and was historically associated with the role of Rex Nemoranses. Typically keep to themselves and are sought out when you need advice the Mother can't or won't give. Offer him your Vitae and he might be willing to tell you things you didn't know you didn't want to know.<br /> <br /> <b>The Crone</b>is an elder member, usually female and always too potent to sustain herself on humans, exists to destroy. She consumes those who have transgressed against The Circle.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Invictus:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Invictus have a TON of titles to denote all sorts of things, from esteem to rank to knightly orders to dynasties to anything else you might want an epithet added to your name for. But as for titles that come with specific duties, they largely conform to the standard positions of power familiar to anyone who's played Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <b>The Prince</b> is the guy in charge.<br /> <br /> <b>The Seneshal</b> is the Prince's second in command.<br /> <br /> <b>The Primogen </b>are a council of advisors to the Prince, often but not always representatives of each prominent covenant within the domain.<br /> <br /> <b>The Prisci</b> (plural: Priscus) are the collective heads of each prominent Clan within the domain.<br /> <br /> <b>The Harpy</b> is a social leader and is sometimes called upon as a propagandist.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sheriff</b> is the guy in charge of enforcing the Prince's laws.<br /> <br /> <b>The Hound</b> or <b>The Scourge</b> is the Sheriff's second in command.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Lancea et Sanctum:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>The Bishop</b> is the religious leader of the local Sanctified.<br /> <br /> <b>The Archbishop</b> is the title used by a Sanctified who rules over a domain (instead of Prince).<br /> <br /> <b>The Cardinal</b> is an extremely rare title used when the Bishop and the Archbishop are the same person.<br /> <br /> <b>Priests</b> perform Theban Sorcery</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Ordo Dracul have a ridiculous number of titles and positions, but unlike the Invictus who seem to do it to promote their own self-importance, the Ordo Dracul is just deliberately trying to be as unnecessarily complicated as possible. They're like one of those secret societies like Skull and Bones that pride themselves on being mysterious and arcane. I won't go into all of the roles here, but it basically boils down to:<br /> <br /> <b>The Sworn of the Axe:</b> are the soldiers and militants.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sworn of the Dying Light:</b> are the scientists and mystics.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sworn of Mysteries:</b> are the judges and politicians.<br /> <br /> Each Sworn has its own system of roles and hierarchies, and each group acts in relative autonomy from the others, though the Sworn of Mysteries are generally the arbiters when conflicts between the different Sworn do arise.<br /> <br /> <b>The Kogaion:</b> is the most important and respected position, but it's almost more of a punishment than an honor to be named Kogaion. They're in charge of mapping leylines, tracking and protecting Wyrm's Nests (locations of mystical power that are of interest to the Order), and generally keeping the Covenant's secrets. They tend to be driven mad from the terrible things they're expected to know and to keep secret.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They're all pretty basic descriptions, and I may have missed a few titles. If you want to know more, the Covenant books are full of this stuff, and most of it is still relevant to second edition.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T04:55:21-07:00","id":474119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=473847#post473847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These stereotypes are very 1st edition. The Covenants have changed somewhat as of 2nd edition.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I based those stereotypes on what I heard about with 2nd edition. The first edition stereotypes suggested that the Lancea Sanctum were just a bunch of penitent vampires, the Circle worshiped a goddess called the Crone, and the Ordo Dracul simply wanted to overcome their weaknesses. So I gave a brief summary of the changes I heard about. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T06:41:39-07:00","id":474237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=474119#post474119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I based those stereotypes on what I heard about with 2nd edition. The first edition stereotypes suggested that the Lancea Sanctum were just a bunch of penitent vampires, the Circle worshiped a goddess called the Crone, and the Ordo Dracul simply wanted to overcome their weaknesses. So I gave a brief summary of the changes I heard about. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Your post made me run to the Requiem 1e corebook and check the Lancea (et) Sanctum section. I...uhm...Yikes! I did not remember it being so vague and bland. That said, I mean the writers no disrespect. It was a huge, daunting task to start from scratch work on WW's flagship title (flagship for being what started the WoD series).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T07:27:50-07:00","id":474280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=474237#post474237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your post made me run to the Requiem 1e corebook and check the Lancea (et) Sanctum section. I...uhm...Yikes! I did not remember it being so vague and bland. That said, I mean the writers no disrespect. It was a huge, daunting task to start from scratch work on WW's flagship title (flagship for being what started the WoD series).</div> </div> </div> </div>A friend of mine who repeatedly voices his &quot;loathing&quot; of NWoD has used &quot;vague and bland&quot; as some of his specific complaints about the setting. I'd wonder if he's only read the 1st Edition core, but he's been reading my Blood &amp; Smoke hard copy, so I doubt that's what it is.<br /> <br /> Still, now I'm interested to check out the 1st Edition book myself, since I never got around to reading it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T08:10:39-07:00","id":474314,"title":"","content":"The covenant books are very dry reading. I had a hard time getting through the ones I wasn't already a fan of. Secrets of the Covenants should spice things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T08:50:19-07:00","id":474342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=474237#post474237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your post made me run to the Requiem 1e corebook and check the Lancea (et) Sanctum section. I...uhm...Yikes! I did not remember it being so vague and bland. That said, I mean the writers no disrespect. It was a huge, daunting task to start from scratch work on WW's flagship title (flagship for being what started the WoD series).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah, it gives fuck all information on Belial's Brood too, which I was really hoping to learn more about, because I think the Sabbat were cool. The entry boils down to &quot;Vampire demon worshipers. Moving on!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:03:09-07:00","id":474353,"title":"","content":"They aren't like the Sabbat, except in embracing ones true Beast.<br /> <br /> You should check out the Belial's Brood book, it's the best covenant book and one of the best supplements in the Requiem line. It really fleshes them out. But, yes, if you just read the core book they're going to be anarchic demon worshipers who want to blow it all up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:04:36-07:00","id":474355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=474280#post474280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A friend of mine who repeatedly voices his &quot;loathing&quot; of NWoD has used &quot;vague and bland&quot; as some of his specific complaints about the setting. I'd wonder if he's only read the 1st Edition core, but he's been reading my Blood &amp; Smoke hard copy, so I doubt that's what it is.<br /> <br /> Still, now I'm interested to check out the 1st Edition book myself, since I never got around to reading it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some folks don't care for the fact that so much in nWoD is left open-ended. There are no hard answers to anything. Where did vampires come from? Everywhere! What caused the fall of the Camarilla? No one remembers! Why do the Strix hate vampires so much? Nobody knows! Just what the heck are VII? Whatever you want them to be!<br /> <br /> I could see that being frustrating to someone who is more interested in playing in a well-defined setting than in using a toolbox to create a setting of their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:16:50-07:00","id":474389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=474355#post474355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some folks don't care for the fact that so much in nWoD is left open-ended. There are no hard answers to anything. Where did vampires come from? Everywhere! What caused the fall of the Camarilla? No one remembers! Why do the Strix hate vampires so much? Nobody knows! Just what the heck are VII? Whatever you want them to be!<br /> <br /> I could see that being frustrating to someone who is more interested in playing in a well-defined setting than in using a toolbox to create a setting of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely a vibe I get from him. It's still annoying, and I often wish I could find that silver bullet that would make him say, &quot;Okay, I guess it's not <i>all</i> bad.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T10:17:00-07:00","id":474461,"title":"","content":"Try shooting him with: less meta game'ing, because now you get to explore the setting together with your character :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:04:17-07:00","id":474524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=474353#post474353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't like the Sabbat, except in embracing ones true Beast.<br /> <br /> You should check out the Belial's Brood book, it's the best covenant book and one of the best supplements in the Requiem line. It really fleshes them out. But, yes, if you just read the core book they're going to be anarchic demon worshipers who want to blow it all up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I know, but the Sabbat were often used as hard core, brutal vampire you should be terrified of, which is what I was comparing them to.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> I for one like the open endedness of the nWoD. I really don't see WHY players need there to be an original vampire or some such crap. Especially with the spontaneous embraces, why can't the reason simply be they've always existed since the dawn of humanity? Besides, there are hundreds of interpretations of vampires scattered all over the world, so an original vampire would have to do a crap load of traveling to have produced them all. As for VII being mysterious, the 1e core book states that not even VII's own members know why they do what they do. Both magical and psychic interrogation has failed to produce any concrete information. So if the covenant itself doesn't know why it exists, it makes sense that it could be up to the ST to determine.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Strix, my head canon is that they are the ghosts of diablerists. Evidence = Black veins in aura of Diablerist. Strix are shadowy, smoke-like beings who feed on vampires and reproduce by splitting themselves. kind of like separating into multiple souls. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> The metaplot was good for an over arching story, but it also gave the setting (by the way, this is imo) a sense of looming dread, and not in the good way. The game was about to end, which means most of the new characters were probably going to die horrible, being too young and inexperienced to build up the power necessary to fight off these ancient horrors that decide to return after thousands of years.<br /> <br /> <br /> The metaplot gave the game a reason for going forward, and brought things to a nice little close. But nWoD is sand boxing it, and gives us the chance to write our own major story lines. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-10-2015, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:21:18-07:00","id":474535,"title":"","content":"Just kiss up to anyone who's more important. If you don't know who that is, don't worry... they're everyone but you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:36:40-07:00","id":474574,"title":"","content":"I think part of the reason a lot of people like the old World of Darkness, aside from it being something they're just used to, is that it tells a story. You can see the various metaplot threads scattered around, and people like connecting the dots or developing favorite characters based on their actions. Obviously not everyone loved it, as one of the complaints I see from fans of the older game is that NPCs often overshadowed characters, so rather than being part of a story they felt like a story was being told over their characters, or did things similarly built characters would find impossible to do. But these are just things I've noticed or heard from people.<br /> <br /> With new World of Darkness, a lot of people seem to think it's just a bare-bones rules system. But the lack of an expansive metaplot isn't the same as a lack of a setting. We obviously have developed NPCs and cities and bloodlines, and characters or events that span into history. But it lacks the feel of a big comprehensive story, and outside of a few, NPCs rarely get the spotlight.<br /> <br /> I always thought they should do more with the signature characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T15:44:53-07:00","id":474981,"title":"","content":"Yes, well unlike oWoD in which everything was tied together, the nWoD games can actually be played as their own separate universes. Just because there are werewolves in Vampire doesn't mean they're spirit detectives patrolling the boundary between worlds. They could just be a bunch of bestial Hulks who really don't like people coming on their land. It's up to the ST to decide whether they're just shapeshifters or Uratha.<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T18:13:19-07:00","id":475147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=474981#post474981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, well unlike oWoD in which everything was tied together, the nWoD games can actually be played as their own separate universes. Just because there are werewolves in Vampire doesn't mean they're spirit detectives patrolling the boundary between worlds. They could just be a bunch of bestial Hulks who really don't like people coming on their land. It's up to the ST to decide whether they're just shapeshifters or Uratha.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think you've got this a bit backwards. Obviously you're free to say &quot;in my game, there are no werewolves&quot; (or the werewolves in my game are XYZ instead of ABC). But the setting material assumes that all the lines do exist in the same world, they just usually keep to themselves. If you do decide otherwise that's totally cool, cause it's a toolbox, but technically it is a deviation from the default assumptions. On the other hand, cWoD was originally written such that the Lupines talked about in Masquerade were not necessarily the Gauru of Apocalypse. I mean, further down the line they did try to tie everything together, but there were already so many contradictory elements between the different lines. That works for nWoD because the contradictions can be resolved by the ST, but in cWoD the metaplot got in the way of that and made it harder to fit everything together in a satisfactory way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T22:28:33-07:00","id":475423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=474524#post474524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I know, but the Sabbat were often used as hard core, brutal vampire you shout be terrified of, which is what I was comparing them to.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From the old forms; Originally there were plans to port the Sabbat into Requiem. It got cut down, and split apart. The majority of the Revised Sabbat is the 1st ed Lancea Sanctum, actually. The &quot;crazy young vampires raising hell and maybe dealing with demons&quot; went to Belial's Brood.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T03:23:31-07:00","id":475585,"title":"","content":"And something like the first edition &quot;mysterious cult we don't know much about&quot; Sabbat shows up in VII.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T05:30:10-07:00","id":475652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=475423#post475423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the old forms; Originally there were plans to port the Sabbat into Requiem. It got cut down, and split apart. The majority of the Revised Sabbat is the 1st ed Lancea Sanctum, actually. The &quot;crazy young vampires raising hell and maybe dealing with demons&quot; went to Belial's Brood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fangs that bite, I was right. I still don't know that much about the Sabbat, but their skewed religious angle reeked of the Lancea Sanctum. Whenever I mentioned it people were like, 'Noooo!' but it fit so well. Thanks for sharing this.<br /> <br /> Belial's Brood got a big expansion in their book, they're made up of numerous factions. The Pandaemonium are the hell raisers, most likely to make shovelheads if such a thing existed. But you also have factions like the Mercy Seat, who corrupt the souls of man so that they can be free of the Gnostic shackles of the Demiurge. Which is a philosophy in the Followers of Set.<br /> <br /> It's probably worth noting as a further comparison to the Sabbat that the Brood practice vaulderie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-10-2015, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T07:07:07-07:00","id":475771,"title":"","content":"Really, the Sabbat was split into multiple parts.<br /> <br /> The Abrahamistic world view (especially represented by the Lasombra's Path of Night) went into the Lance et Sanctum<br /> The focus on transcendence and metamorphosis of the Tzimisce went into the Ordo Dracul<br /> The visceral, mindless brutality, appreciation of the Beast and infernalism went into Belial's Brood (some of them, at any rate)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T17:30:27-07:00","id":476463,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd love to see VtR completely get over Masquerade and do its own stuff. In doing so, it will definitely repeat some of the same mistakes from VtM, but at least it won't be out of trying to hard to imitate or avoid imitating Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Ideal scenario would be to get a series of books with VtR metaplot (a grand Strix invasion, complete with Strix domains in the Shadow Realms), new fiction, and insane setting stuff that create a concrete world with an actual, detailed history. Put a sidebar in the beginning that say that you don't have to use all this stuff, and watch them sell like hotcakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T17:44:20-07:00","id":476472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=476463#post476463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd love to see VtR completely get over Masquerade and do its own stuff. In doing so, it will definitely repeat some of the same mistakes from VtM, but at least it won't be out of trying to hard to imitate or avoid imitating Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good news! This book exists, it's called Vampire: the Requiem, Second Edition and it is available in PDF and POD on DrivethruRPG.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=476463#post476463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideal scenario would be to get a series of books with VtR metaplot (a grand Strix invasion, complete with Strix domains in the Shadow Realms), new fiction, and insane setting stuff that create a concrete world with an actual, detailed history. Put a sidebar in the beginning that say that you don't have to use all this stuff, and watch them sell like hotcakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Strix Chronicle featured in 2nd edition <i>does</i> have a concrete setting and actual, detailed history, not to mention a companion fiction anthology. It does not, will not, and should not contain a metaplot (i.e. canonical events that occur after year 0 and have significant impact on the setting) because that would alienate the nWoD fanbase, for many of whom the lack of metaplot is a key selling point. Clear &quot;THIS IS OPTIONAL&quot; tags would not be sufficient for a significant portion of the 'base. The Strix Chronicle is already more of a compromise than a lot of fans were comfortable with, and had to go a long way to reassure them that more fleshed out setting details and history =/= metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T19:41:26-07:00","id":476506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=474355#post474355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some folks don't care for the fact that so much in nWoD is left open-ended. There are no hard answers to anything. Where did vampires come from? Everywhere! What caused the fall of the Camarilla? No one remembers! Why do the Strix hate vampires so much? Nobody knows! Just what the heck are VII? Whatever you want them to be!<br /> <br /> I could see that being frustrating to someone who is more interested in playing in a well-defined setting than in using a toolbox to create a setting of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ^Me^<br /> <br /> While I'm not averse to a sandbox setting, Req 1.0 wasn't even that. Req 1.0 was a load of rough timber, eight or ten fifty-pound sandbags, and a couple dozen carpentry tools still in theft-proof plastic. Ask for a set of plans and people looked at you like you were a fucking lunatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T20:41:51-07:00","id":476570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=476506#post476506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ^Me^<br /> <br /> While I'm not averse to a sandbox setting, Req 1.0 wasn't even that. Req 1.0 was a load of rough timber, eight or ten fifty-pound sandbags, and a couple dozen carpentry tools still in theft-proof plastic. Ask for a set of plans and people looked at you like you were a fucking lunatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's a toolbox, not a sandbox. As I said, the Strix Chronicle in 2e provides a nice, more fleshed out setting. There are still some blanks to be filled in (it wouldn't be nWoD if there weren't) but it is far better than the 1e core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T20:56:41-07:00","id":476582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=476472#post476472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good news! This book exists, it's called Vampire: the Requiem, Second Edition and it is available in PDF and POD on DrivethruRPG.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>By the way, what does PDF and POD mean? I've been tempted to buy the books from DriveThru as it seems it would make playing with others much easier. But it has the options for PDF, soft cover and hard cover. Which leads me to believe PDF means you download the book instead of having it delivered, which I feel could be too easily lost. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T21:04:29-07:00","id":476606,"title":"","content":"PDF is a file format, they're downloadable versions you can put on your computer and move to any computer. Providing you have an account with DrivethruRPG, they'll let you download it again and again if you remove it from your computer. POD means print on demand, its how they make Onyx Path books now, outside of the Deluxe and Premium editions from Kickstarter. Essentially you buy a print book from DrivethruRPG, they use their own printer and make the book, then send it to you.<br /> <br /> It's surprisingly quick, but apparently I'm nearby or something, delivery has never been very long for me and I understand its been a while for others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-11-2015, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T21:09:02-07:00","id":476612,"title":"","content":"Oh, that's good if they link the book to your account. I was afraid if your computer crashed or something, you had to buy it again... kind of like the DLC for Dragon Age!<br /> <br /> I managed to buy Core, Vamp, and Werewolf books at Barnes and Noble at the mall, but it looks like they only had 1 copy of each. I wondered why nobody bought them for months on end... then I found out they were 1e rules after I purchased them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Wish I had bought Mage or Changeling though, I don't live close enough to revisit now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T21:18:18-07:00","id":476616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=476612#post476612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, that's good if they link the book to your account. I was afraid if your computer crashed or something, you had to buy it again... kind of like the DLC for Dragon Age!<br /> <br /> I managed to buy Core, Vamp, and Werewolf books at Barnes and Noble at the mall, but it looks like they only had 1 copy of each. I wondered why nobody bought them for months on end... then I found out they were 1e rules after I purchased them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Wish I had bought Mage or Changeling though, I don't live close enough to revisit now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Onyx Path is all Print on Demand and PDF download now, so book stores and gaming stores aren't going to carry their books, unless they have leftover copies from when White Wolf used to do traditional printing. Anything new, you'll have to order from Drivethru RPG. I like to get the PDF + POD combos - it's a little cheaper than buying both individually, and I then I have the digital copy on my computer and tablet if I need to look something up on the move (and to read while I wait for the physical copy to print and ship) and a physical copy for my bookshelf and for passing around the gaming table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T23:37:50-07:00","id":476716,"title":"","content":"You don't have to buy again DLC of Dragon Age if your computer crashes, at least if you're buying it with Origin. Mine computer crashed and I didn't have to buy again any DLC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T01:17:47-07:00","id":476764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=476716#post476716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to buy again DLC of Dragon Age if your computer crashes, at least if you're buying it with Origin. Mine computer crashed and I didn't have to buy again any DLC.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When we first bought the game, we got a code to unlock the Shale DLC for free. Computer crashed, forcing us to completely reinstal it, and when I signed into my account again, it demanded we buy the DLC. Couldn't use the code either, because it had already been spent. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> Actually, I believe my Werewolf book is still up to date, isn't it? Or have they released 2e Werewolf? I thought it was still being worked on last I heard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T03:36:39-07:00","id":476822,"title":"","content":"It is already done, at least the advanced pdf (pre-errata). The pdf with the errata corrected will be available in a month or so. If you buy the advanced you get the corrected pdf for free when available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T07:28:56-07:00","id":476933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=476570#post476570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's a toolbox, not a sandbox. As I said, the Strix Chronicle in 2e provides a nice, more fleshed out setting. There are still some blanks to be filled in (it wouldn't be nWoD if there weren't) but it is far better than the 1e core.</div> </div> </div> </div>VtR 2e covered 120% of my gripes with 1e core. I got my premium hardcover that says Blood and Smoke on it and love it even more for this reason. My point was that, should an interesting story arc for a &quot;metaplot&quot; (aka a whole book containing a single SAS) come up, I would like writers to go to town with it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T07:46:19-07:00","id":476940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/473626-could-anyone-please-give-me-a-quick-rundown-of-kindred-politics-in-2ed?p=476933#post476933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VtR 2e covered 120% of my gripes with 1e core. I got my premium hardcover that says Blood and Smoke on it and love it even more for this reason. My point was that, should an interesting story arc for a &amp;quot;metaplot&amp;quot; (aka a whole book containing a single SAS) come up, I would like writers to go to town with it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is a pretty neat idea, if presented as an adventure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}